@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Bitmap CMYK output
+
+Bitmaps > Mode > CMYK stores a per-object output model through the command
+engine. Convert to Bitmap > CMYK sets the same model on the new bitmap.
+The PNG is retained as the lossless RGB source and preview, including alpha.
+The document's primary color mode alone never changes an imported bitmap.
+
+Normal PDF export converts the selected CMYK bitmap's RGB samples through
+`Color::convert_to("CMYK")`, the same working color engine as vector colors,
+and quantizes each channel by `round(clamp(channel, 0, 1) * 255)`.
+The image stream has four samples per pixel and `/DeviceCMYK`. Alpha is kept
+as a separate `/DeviceGray` soft mask. RGB bitmaps remain `/DeviceRGB`.
+The output mode is stored in native drawings and participates in undo/redo.
+RGB mode restores output from the original RGB source, without another lossy
+CMYK-to-RGB conversion. This is output conversion, not CMYK PNG encoding;
+PNG has no CMYK pixel format. SVG still carries an RGB preview.
+
+Raster edits retain the output model and reconvert the updated pixels at
+export. A fixed output profile must be selected before final export when
+specific press values are required. CDR and SVG preservation of this new
+per-object output mode is not claimed by this change.
+
+Regression coverage: `crates/io/tests/bitmap_cmyk.rs`, and the bitmap mode menu
+and Convert to Bitmap tests in `apps/tracedraw/src/ops2.rs`.
